WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.930
Now the code, in two pieces: a PowerShell
run that reads the tenant, and new

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:10.388
Python files beside the first workbook's
drift pipeline, which stays unchanged.

3
00:00:10.388 --> 00:00:12.212
The design has three parts.

4
00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:15.226
Chapters 1 and 2 describe
the tenant's state.

5
00:00:15.226 --> 00:00:18.125
The audit read describes
the events in a window.

6
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:21.712
And comparing with the last
run turns state into drift.

7
00:00:21.712 --> 00:00:23.866
Chain those windows with no gaps,

8
00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:27.137
and you have every elevation
in the period, in code.

9
00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:31.774
Each run writes one folder, with
a run file that records the cloud,

10
00:00:31.774 --> 00:00:35.260
tenant, window and a hash
of each task's manifest.
